Findings
- **Where `xwin` appears**
 - `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CargoBuildMojo.java`
 - `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CargoTestMojo.java`
 - Both define the Maven property and selection logic:
 ```java
 @Parameter(property = "xWin", defaultValue = "false")
 private boolean xWin;
 ...
 private String getToolchain() {
 if (cross) { return "cross"; }
 if (xWin) { return "xwin"; }
 return null;
 }
 ```
 - To enable `xwin` from CLI: pass `-DxWin=true` (or set `<xWin>true</xWin>` in plugin config). The `cross` option is `-Dcross=true`.

- **How `toolchain` is used / what to pass**
 - `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/Crate.java` contains:
 ```java
 public void build(String toolchain) { 
 List<String> args = new ArrayList<>();
 if (toolchain != null) { args.add(toolchain); }
 args.add("build");
 addCargoArgs(args);
 cargo(args);
 }
 public void test(String toolchain) { ... }
 ```
 - The plugin prepends the `toolchain` string as the first argument to the cargo subcommand. Effectively the executed command is:
 - `[cargoPath] [toolchain?] build ...`
 - Example: `cargo xwin build --target-dir ...` if `toolchain == "xwin"`.
 - That means `xwin` is passed as a cargo subcommand/name placed before `build`/`test` (so it must be resolvable as a command/subcommand in the environment or be a cargo subcommand wrapper).

- **Other relevant Maven properties (from `CargoMojoBase.java`)**
 - `path` (required) — crate path
 - `skip` — skip execution
 - `cargoPath` — path to cargo (default `cargo`)
 - `release` — `--release`
 - `target` — `--target`
 - `features`, `all-features`, `no-default-features`
 - `verbosity` (`-q`, `-v`, `-vv`)
 - `extra-args`, `environmentVariables`
 - These are forwarded into the cargo invocation via `addCargoArgs(...)`.

What this means for you
- To use `xwin` enable the `xWin` property: `mvn ... -DxWin=true`.
- If you want `cross` instead: `mvn ... -Dcross=true`.
- If you need to pass a custom toolchain executable name, the plugin will insert that string before `build`/`test` in the cargo command (so ensure the toolchain is on PATH or set `cargoPath` accordingly).

Changes made
- None (read-only inspection).

If you want, I can:
