Where cargo is executed
- File: `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/Crate.java`
- The high-level flow:
 - `cargo(List<String> args)` builds the full command (calls `getCargoPath()` to get `cargoPath`, prepends it, logs it) then calls `runCommand(cmd)`.
 - `runCommand(List<String> args)` uses `ProcessBuilder` to start the process, redirects output, sets environment and working directory, streams stdout to the plugin log, waits for completion, and throws on non-zero exit.

Relevant code (from `Crate.java`):
```java
private void cargo(List<String> args) throws MojoExecutionException, MojoFailureException {
 String cargoPath = getCargoPath();
 final List<String> cmd = new ArrayList<>();
 cmd.add(cargoPath);
 cmd.addAll(args);
 log.info("Working directory: " + crateRoot);
 ...
 log.info("Running: " + Shlex.quote(cmd));
 try {
 runCommand(cmd);
 } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
 CargoInstalledChecker.INSTANCE.check(cargoPath);
 throw new MojoFailureException("Failed to invoke cargo", e);
 }
}
```

```java
private void runCommand(List<String> args)
 throws IOException, InterruptedException, MojoExecutionException {
 final ProcessBuilder processBuilder = new ProcessBuilder(args);
 processBuilder.redirectErrorStream(true);
 processBuilder.environment().putAll(params.environmentVariables);
 processBuilder.directory(crateRoot.toFile());
 final Process process = processBuilder.start();
 Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor().submit(() ->
 new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()))
 .lines()
 .forEach(log::info));
 final int exitCode = process.waitFor();
 if (exitCode != 0) {
 throw new MojoExecutionException(
 "Cargo command failed with exit code " + exitCode);
 }
}
```

Extra details
- `getCargoPath()` expands `~` on non-Windows and returns `params.cargoPath` (default `"cargo"`), so the executed binary is whatever `cargoPath` points to.
- If a toolchain string is supplied (e.g., `"xwin"`), it is inserted as the first argument in `args` before `build`/`test`, so the actual executed command looks like: `[cargoPath] xwin build ...` (or `[cargoPath] build ...` if toolchain is null).

Summary
- The cargo invocation is assembled in `cargo(...)` and actually executed by `runCommand(...)` in `Crate.java`.
- `ProcessBuilder.start()` runs the process; stdout is streamed to the Maven log; non-zero exit causes a `MojoExecutionException`."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
