Proposed plan (verify to continue)
```
[ ] Add a new Maven parameter `xWinCrossCompiler` (property `xWinCrossCompiler`) to `CargoMojoBase`
[ ] Default the parameter value to "clang-cl" and validate allowed values ("clang-cl","clang") in `getCommonCrateParams()`
[ ] Add a field `crossCompiler` to `Crate.Params` and populate it from `getCommonCrateParams()`
[ ] Modify `Crate.build(String toolchain)` and `Crate.test(String toolchain)` so:
 - if toolchain equals "xwin", prepend the toolchain as now AND
 - insert `--cross-compiler <value>` into the cargo args (before `build`/`test`), using `params.crossCompiler`
 - do NOT add the flag for other toolchains
[ ] Add unit tests in `rust-maven-plugin/src/test/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CrateTest.java`:
 - Create a temp script as `params.cargoPath` that records its argv to a file and exits 0
 - Call `crate.build("xwin")` with `params.crossCompiler="clang"` and assert the recorded argv contains `xwin`, `--cross-compiler`, `clang`, and `build` in expected order
 - Call `crate.build("cross")` (or `null`) and assert `--cross-compiler` is NOT present
 - Test default (when param unset) results in `clang-cl` being passed for `xwin`
[ ] Run the unit tests and fix any issues (ensure tests are robust on CI; scripts use `/bin/sh`)

Notes / decisions
- I propose putting the new property on `CargoMojoBase` so both `build` and `test` mojos inherit it.
- Validation will throw `MojoExecutionException` for invalid values.
- Tests will avoid calling real `cargo` by pointing `params.cargoPath` to a small executable script that writes its argv to a file and returns 0.
- The `--cross-compiler` flag will only be added when the toolchain argument equals `"xwin"`.

Do you approve this plan? If yes I will implement the changes and run the tests."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
