What I changed (high-level)
- Added a new Maven parameter on `CargoMojoBase`:
 - `xWinCrossCompiler` (`-DxWinCrossCompiler=...`) with default `"clang-cl"`, validated to accept only `"clang-cl"` or `"clang"`.
- Threaded the value into `Crate.Params` as `crossCompiler`.
- Updated `Crate.build(...)` and `Crate.test(...)` to inject `--cross-compiler <value>` immediately after the `build`/`test` subcommand when the toolchain is `"xwin"`.
 - This yields invocations like: `cargo xwin build --cross-compiler clang --target ...`
- Added unit tests in `rust-maven-plugin/src/test/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CrateTest.java`:
 - `testXwinCrossCompilerArgPassed` verifies the `--cross-compiler` arg and ordering when `xwin` is used.
 - `testNoCrossCompilerForNonXwin` verifies the flag is not present for other toolchains.
 - Tests use a temporary wrapper script as `params.cargoPath` to capture the actual argv passed.

Files changed
- `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CargoMojoBase.java` — added parameter and validation
- `rust-maven-plugin/src/main/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/Crate.java` — added `crossCompiler` to `Params` and inject args for `xwin`
- `rust-maven-plugin/src/test/java/io/questdb/maven/rust/CrateTest.java` — added two tests verifying behavior

Test run result
- I attempted to run `mvn -Dtest=CrateTest test` but Maven is not installed in this environment (`mvn: command not found`). You can run the tests locally with:
 - `mvn -Dtest=CrateTest test | cat`

