- Enable xwin: pass `-DxWin=true` (or set `<xWin>true</xWin>` in plugin `<configuration>`).
- Choose cross-compiler (allowed values: **`clang-cl`** (default) or **`clang`**): pass `-DxWinCrossCompiler=clang` (or `<xWinCrossCompiler>clang</xWinCrossCompiler>`).
- Other common properties: `-Dpath=<crate-path>`, `-Dtarget=<rust-triple>`, `-Drelease=true`, `-DcargoPath=<path-to-cargo>`.

Examples

- CLI (one-off):
 - Build with xwin using clang:
 mvn -Dpath=rust/crate -DxWin=true -DxWinCrossCompiler=clang -Dtarget=x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -Drelease=true package | cat
 - Run tests with xwin:
 mvn -Dpath=rust/crate -DxWin=true -DxWinCrossCompiler=clang test | cat

- In `pom.xml` plugin configuration:
```xml
<configuration>
 <path>rust/crate</path>
 <xWin>true</xWin>
 <xWinCrossCompiler>clang</xWinCrossCompiler>
 <target>x86_64-pc-windows-msvc</target>
 <release>true</release>
</configuration>
```

What the plugin will execute
- For `xWin=true` the plugin inserts the toolchain and the flag; the executed command will look like:
 `cargo xwin build --cross-compiler clang --target <target> --release --target-dir <...> ...`
- For non-`xwin` toolchains (e.g., `cross`) the `--cross-compiler` flag is NOT added.

Notes
- Valid `xWinCrossCompiler` values: `clang-cl` (default) or `clang`. Invalid values cause a Maven configuration error.
- If `cargo` is not on PATH or you want a wrapper, set `-DcargoPath=/path/to/cargo_or_wrapper`.
- Use `-Dpath` to point to the crate manifest directory (or set it in plugin config).

If you want, I can:
- Add an example in the repo README showing these commands, or
- Show the exact command produced for your crate if you give me `path` and `target`."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
